Changes made by Humanjava Enterprises (Apache-2.0, section 4(b)):
- Converted the language-model weights to GGUF; the vision encoder is not included.
- v2: quantized the weights to standard llama.cpp K-quant mixes (Q4_K_M, Q3_K_M)
  with an importance matrix computed on English, French and Québec French text,
  including text written by the original model. No fine-tuning.
- v2: replaced the embedded chat template with one that has thinking off by
  default (the original template's enable_thinking=false path).
- v1: quantized the weights to a mix of standard llama.cpp 2- to 4-bit block
  types, then further calibrated and trained the quantized weights on English
  and French text, including text written by the original model, so the
  outputs stay close to the original's in both languages.

